T*
/F1 8 Tf
(  # Report) Tj
T*
(  Yihao Yin \(yihaoyin\)) Tj
T*
(  ) Tj
T*
(  Forecasting the Tennessee Eastman stripper temperature `xmeas_18` \(deg C\) 1 to 40 samples \(3 to 120 min\)) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(ahead. `uv run python src/pipeline.py` rebuilds every file in `results/`, byte-identical on rerun.) Tj
T*
(  ) Tj
T*
(  ## 1. The table) Tj
T*
(  `build_table\(df, h, n_lags\)` in `src/table.py` returns one row per \(run, t\): the lags y[t], y[t-1], ...,) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(y[t-n_lags+1] of `xmeas_18`, the valves `xmv_1` to `xmv_11` at sample t, and the target y[t+h]. All but) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(the target is known at t; the valves are taken at t only, since later moves are not known when the) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(forecast is made. Every lag and the target is `pl.col\(Y\).shift\(k\).over\(RUN, order_by=SAMPLE\)`, so each) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(shift restarts in each run and gives null at its edges instead of reading the neighbouring run. Those) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(rows are dropped, and origins start at t = 40, so every lag depth up to 40 is scored on the same rows.) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(`load\(\)` checks that every run holds samples 1 to 500 exactly once, so a shift by k rows is a shift by) Tj
T*
(      ) Tj
(k samples. Checked against a per-run array, every lag, valve and target is `xmeas_18` at t-k, t and t+h) Tj
T*
